CHAPTER XI — TECH TREES & PROGRESSION
Progression in Obsidian Protocol is built around research, upgrades, veterancy, and experimental unlocks.
These systems allow players to evolve their faction, enhance squads, unlock advanced units, and shape the strategic direction of each match.

This chapter defines:

Research mechanics

Unit upgrades

Building upgrades

Veterancy

Faction tech trees

Experimental unlocks

11.1 Research
Research unlocks new units, abilities, upgrades, and command actions.

Research Sources
Research Lab — primary research building

Insight — sensor‑based research boosts

Archive — data‑driven research acceleration

Worldmap — terrain‑based research unlocks

Vector Core — experimental research

Research Types
Research Type	Unlocks
Unit Research	New units, variants, specialties
Weapon Research	New payloads, ammo types, damage upgrades
Armor Research	Armor tiers, shield systems
Sensor Research	LIDAR, thermal, stealth detection
Command Research	Leadership abilities, radius boosts
Logistics Research	Supply chain efficiency, repair speed
Experimental Research	Superweapons, teleportation, gravity manipulation


Research Rules
Requires resources

Requires power grid stability

Requires building prerequisites

Can be queued

Can be accelerated by command abilities

Research AI Behavior
AI may autonomously:

Suggest research based on battlefield needs

Prioritize counter‑unit research

Delay research during hazards

Boost research during stable phases

11.2 Unit Upgrades
Unit upgrades enhance stats, unlock abilities, and improve battlefield performance.

Upgrade Categories
Offensive Upgrades — damage, accuracy, rate of fire

Defensive Upgrades — armor, shields, evasion

Mobility Upgrades — speed, maneuverability

Sensor Upgrades — visibility cones, detection

Specialty Upgrades — breach tools, stealth, suppression

Logistics Upgrades — ammo capacity, reload speed

Upgrade Rules
Require research

Require resources

Apply globally or per unit type

Stack with veterancy

May unlock new intent behaviors

Upgrade Effects
Upgrades may:

Improve autonomous decision‑making

Enhance breach logic

Increase flanking effectiveness

Reduce retreat likelihood

Improve coordination

11.3 Building Upgrades
Building upgrades improve production, efficiency, durability, and command capabilities.

Building Upgrade Types
Production Speed

Queue Capacity

Power Efficiency

Sensor Range

Command Radius

Logistics Throughput

Durability & Repair Rate

Upgrade Rules
Require tech tree unlocks

Require resources

Require stable power grid

May require command unit presence

Building Upgrade AI Behavior
AI may:

Recommend upgrades

Delay upgrades during hazards

Prioritize Command Core upgrades

Balance upgrades across infrastructure

11.4 Veterancy
Veterancy represents unit experience gained through combat.

Veterancy Levels
Level	Name	Effects
I	Trained	Minor stat boosts
II	Hardened	Improved accuracy, reduced suppression
III	Veteran	Enhanced abilities, faster intent execution
IV	Elite	Major stat boosts, unique behaviors
V	Legendary	Unique bonuses, morale aura


Veterancy Effects
Veterancy improves:

Accuracy

Evasion

Morale

Initiative

Breach performance

Flanking behavior

Retreat thresholds

Veterancy Loss
If a squad is destroyed, veterancy is lost permanently.

11.5 Faction Tech Trees
Each faction has a unique tech tree defining its strategic identity.
For the Warden Program (your first playable faction), the tech tree emphasizes:

Autonomous coordination

Sensor superiority

Precision strikes

Logistics efficiency

Experimental integration

Tech Tree Structure
The Warden tech tree is divided into four branches:

1. Tactical Branch
Unlocks:

Squad abilities

Breach tools

Suppression upgrades

Autonomous coordination boosts

2. Strategic Branch
Unlocks:

Command abilities

Radius boosts

Morale upgrades

Initiative surges

3. Logistics Branch
Unlocks:

Supply chain efficiency

Repair speed

Power grid upgrades

Drone enhancements

4. Experimental Branch
Unlocks:

Echo

Nullpoint

Specter

Shadowgrid

Phantom

Helix

Vector Core abilities

Tech Tree Rules
Branches can be pursued independently

Some nodes require cross‑branch prerequisites

Experimental branch requires rare resources

Tech tree choices shape late‑game identity

11.6 Experimental Unlocks
Experimental unlocks represent the pinnacle of progression.

Unlock Requirements
High‑tier research

Rare experimental resources

Vector Core activation

Command Core level threshold

Stable power grid

Logistics chain integrity

Experimental Unlock Types
Superweapons — gravity wells, energy storms

Teleportation — squad redeploy

Cloaking Fields — stealth zones

Hazard Manipulation — fire, radiation, EMP

Terrain Reshaping — collapse, elevation shifts

Quantum Units — Echo, Nullpoint, Phantom

Experimental AI Behavior
Experimental units:

Ignore standard terrain rules

Use abilities to reshape battlefield

Coordinate with command units

Retreat when cooldowns are active

Avoid detection until strike moment

Experimental unlocks define the late‑game spectacle.
